											]
										},
										"description": "### PATCH /kader/presensi-ibk/update/{id}\n\nThis endpoint is used to update the attendance status of a specific user identified by their unique ID. The request modifies the attendance status for the user in the system.\n\n#### Request Parameters\n\n- **Path Parameter**\n    \n    - `id` (string): The unique identifier of the attendance record that you want to update. In this example, the ID presensi is `eaa719ea-13ef-4fe6-8c0b-262ed70a9871`.\n        \n- **Request Body**\n    \n    - `status_presensi` (string): The new attendance status for the user. This parameter accepts values such as `\"BELUM_HADIR,HADIR,SAKIT,IZIN\"` to indicate that the user has not attended.\n        \n\n#### Example Request Body\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"status_presensi\": \"BELUM_HADIR\"\n}\n\n ```\n\n#### Response Structure\n\nUpon a successful update, the server responds with a status code of `200` and a JSON object containing the following fields:\n\n- `id` (string): The unique identifier of the attendance record.\n    \n- `user_ibk_id` (string): The ID of the user whose attendance status has been updated.\n    \n- `jadwal_id` (string): The ID of the schedule associated with the attendance record.\n    \n- `status_presensi` (string): The updated attendance status.\n    \n- `created_at` (string): The timestamp when the attendance record was created.\n    \n- `updated_at` (string): The timestamp when the attendance record was last updated.\n    \n- `deleted_at` (null): Indicates if the record has been deleted (null if not deleted).\n    \n\n#### Example Response\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"id\": \"\",\n  \"user_ibk_id\": \"\",\n  \"jadwal_id\": \"\",\n  \"status_presensi\": \"\",\n  \"created_at\": \"\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"\",\n  \"deleted_at\": null\n}\n\n ```\n\nThis endpoint allows for efficient management of attendance records, ensuring that the status can be updated as needed."
									},
